instr:
Support template slide editing and inspection in `@office-kit/pptx`

Our presentation tooling needs to edit template decks and inspect their layouts and shapes before export. Complete the existing free-function API for layout discovery, preset shape authoring, geometry queries and edits, hyperlinks, image backgrounds, speaker notes, and slide indices and dimensions.

For example, adding speaker notes to an existing deck should look like this:

```ts
import { appendSlideNotes, getSlides, loadPresentation, savePresentation, setSlideNotes } from '@office-kit/pptx';
const deck = await loadPresentation(templateBytes);
const slide = getSlides(deck)[0]!;
setSlideNotes(slide, 'Confirm the launch date.');
appendSlideNotes(slide, 'Leave time for questions.');
const updatedBytes = await savePresentation(deck);
```

These operations should support editing and inspecting a deck, with authored changes preserved through saving and loading. The expected behaviour is described in the doc comments on the unfinished declarations and `README.md`'s “Usage” section.

Currently, stubs throw `new Error("not implemented")` in the following files, relative to the package root:

